        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> As I said on Reddit, this module is fantastic. The _only_ thing I think could be improved is, when calling `:write`, test for the `background` value to preserve the original colorscheme file's light/dark variants.\r\n> \r\n> (Just wanted to put it here, since a forum isn't the best place to track those things)\r\n\r\nThanks for the feedback!\r\n\r\nNot exactly sure what you mean here. If you mean creating a file which checks for `'background'` and sources either one of the color schemes, then no it doesn't do that. And I don't think this is reasonable in the scope of this module.\r\n\r\nGeneral idea is that color scheme is basically a set of name, highlight group definitions, and terminal colors. Imagine like a snapshot: nothing conditional, only preserve the state.\r\n\r\nIf you want to make a color scheme with different highlights depending on the value of 'background' (which is totally reasonable), I'd suggest creating three variants of color scheme: `scheme_dark`, `scheme_light`, and `scheme` which conditionally sources either one depending on 'background'\r\n\r\nI'll keep this \"conditional on `'background'`\" in mind. Maybe I'll find a reasonable way to add this.",
            "created_at": "2023-04-17T08:32:39Z",
